<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="ae55d087">Materials that will prepare meeting participants for the content, purpose, and expectations of the scheduled meeting
so that participants are brought up to speed on the related topics and may formulate questions beforehand.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="fa9c6f7d"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="f9e56de4"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="4931d6d4"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="3630e03a">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of the agenda is to provide invitees with the necessary information to make the actual meeting as
    productive as possible and serves as a basis for conducting the actual meeting.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Using a well-thought-out meeting agenda for client meetings supports delivery of superior, consistent service quality
    in that it contributes to effective management of client expectations and communications.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="e8b081e8">Without a set agenda it is unlikely that the required topics will be covered, and it is more likely that time will be
wasted during the meeting.</attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="b70a92a5">Ad hoc meetings or those limited to discussing a single subject may not require this work product.</attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="99b5774">&lt;p&gt;
    At a minimum it should  include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        A set time and location that is agreed upon by all participating parties
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        An invite of the meeting
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        A prioritized list of discussion topics including estimated time, durations, and presenters
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Other items to consider including consist of the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Planned time and date
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        List of invitees
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Meeting objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Discussion topics
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        List of pre-read or background materials
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="eeca2b04">&lt;p&gt;
    If possible, this work product should be maintained in the selected meeting scheduling tool.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
